;IN CHAIN A, IT WAS NOT POSSIBLE TO UNAMBIGUOUSLY DETERMINE THE SEQUENCE
 REGISTER FOR RESIDUES 697 TO 747. THESE RESIDUES ARE THEREFORE DESIGNATED
 UNK TO INDICATE THIS AMBIGUITY.  IN CHAIN E,  RESIDUES 86 TO 121 ARE GIVEN
 THE AMINO ACID TYPES THAT CORRESPOND TO THE GENE NUMBERING,  HOWEVER THE 
SEQUENCE REGISTER MAY BE INCORRECT DUE TO A LACK OF DENSITY FOR FLANKING LOOPS.
;
_refine.pdbx_starting_model                      '1PLQ, 1JR3, 1NJF, 1IQP' 
